    <bpmn:process id="W_W1414" name="W1414. Customer Trade Account Credit Insurance Premium Review, Claims Filing &amp; Recovery Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual policy renewal; quarterly premium review; or trade account write-off event (W81) triggering insurance claim
Frequency: Annual policy renewal; quarterly premium reconciliation; claims as needed (estimated 5–10 claims/year for accounts written off &gt; PHP 500,000)
Volume: ~5,200 trade accounts insured under group credit insurance policy; ~5–10 claims/year for significant bad debts
Owner: AR Supervisor
Participants: AR Supervisor, Controller, CFO, Credit Insurance Underwriter, Insurance Broker, VP Legal
Source: workflow W1414 — Customer Trade Account Credit Insurance Premium Review, Claims Filing &amp; Recovery Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1414_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1414_Lane1" name="AR Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1414_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1414_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1414_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1414_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1414_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1414_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1414_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1414_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1414_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1414_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1414_Lane2" name="Underwriter">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1414_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1414_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1414_Start4" name="Annual policy renewal; quarterly premium review; or trade account write-off event (W81)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1414_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1414_Task5" name="Policy selection and renewal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Policy selection and renewal: annually, AR Supervisor and Controller evaluate credit insurance options: (a) review current policy coverage (% of receivable insured, maximum tenor, country/customer exclusions), (b) obtain competitive quotes from 2–3 underwriters, (c) negotiate premium rate (typically 0.15–0.40% of insured receivable volume), (d) CFO approves policy selection and premium budget; policy covers 80% of approved receivable balances up to a portfolio limit
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor / Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1414_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1414_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1414_Task6" name="Customer coverage submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Customer coverage submission: AR Supervisor submits the complete trade account portfolio to the underwriter for coverage assessment: (a) each customer&#x27;s credit limit request (aligned with BuildRight&#x27;s internal credit limits per W24), (b) customer financial statements (for corporate accounts &gt; PHP 5M credit limit), (c) payment history (aging and days sales outstanding per customer), (d) industry risk classification; underwriter approves, reduces, or declines coverage per customer
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Underwriter
Duration: 1 week/annual cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1414_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1414_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1414_Task7" name="Quarterly premium reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quarterly premium reconciliation: AR Supervisor reconciles quarterly premium invoice from underwriter: (a) premium = insured receivable balance at quarter-end × premium rate, (b) verify insured receivable balance matches AR sub-ledger, (c) verify no premium charged for cash/advance-payment customers, (d) submit premium invoice for payment per W7; typical annual premium at 0.25% rate on ~PHP 500M average insured AR = ~PHP 1.25M/year
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1414_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1414_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1414_Task8" name="New customer coverage request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: New customer coverage request: when a new trade account is onboarded (W460) or an existing account&#x27;s credit limit is increased (W1300), AR Supervisor submits a coverage request to the underwriter: (a) customer name and TIN, (b) requested credit limit, (c) customer trade references, (d) payment terms; underwriter responds within 5–10 business days with approved coverage limit
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min/request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1414_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1414_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1414_Task9" name="Claim filing — protracted default">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Claim filing — protracted default: when a trade account is identified for write-off (W81) after exhaustion of collection efforts (W108, W812): (a) AR Supervisor gathers claim documentation: original invoice copies, delivery receipts, proof of demand letters, statement of account, collection history log, customer TIN and registration, (b) submits claim to underwriter within policy notification period (typically 60–90 days from due date or 180 days from invoice date), (c) AR Supervisor certifies that BuildRight has complied with all policy conditions (collection efforts, notice of overdue, retention of title if applicable)
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 4–8 hours/claim</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1414_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1414_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1414_Task10" name="Claim filing — insolvency/bankruptcy">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Claim filing — insolvency/bankruptcy: if a trade account customer files for bankruptcy or is placed under receivership: (a) VP Legal provides court filing documentation, (b) AR Supervisor submits claim with proof of insolvency (court order, SEC petition, published notice), (c) claim must be filed within 30 days of knowledge of insolvency event per most policy terms
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–8 hours/claim</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1414_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1414_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1414_Task11" name="Underwriter reviews claim: (a) verifies customer was covered under policy at…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Underwriter reviews claim: (a) verifies customer was covered under policy at time of sale, (b) verifies credit limit was not exceeded, (c) verifies BuildRight complied with notification requirements, (d) may request additional documentation or conduct independent investigation; claim processing time: 30–90 days
Responsible (R): Underwriter
Accountable (A): —
Duration: External</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1414_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1414_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1414_Task12" name="Claim settlement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Claim settlement: underwriter approves claim and pays indemnity: 80% of approved receivable (per policy terms); AR Supervisor receives payment, posts to GL: Dr. Cash / Cr. Credit Insurance Recovery (other income); remaining 20% uninsured portion remains as BuildRight&#x27;s loss per W81
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor / Treasury
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1414_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1414_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1414_Task13" name="Subrogation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Subrogation: if the customer later pays (full or partial), BuildRight must remit the proportional recovery to the underwriter per subrogation clause; AR Supervisor tracks subrogation obligations in system
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min/recovery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1414_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1414_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1414_Task14" name="Annual policy performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Annual policy performance review: AR Supervisor prepares credit insurance scorecard for CFO: (a) total premiums paid, (b) total claims filed, (c) total claims recovered, (d) net cost/benefit of insurance, (e) policy loss ratio (claims/premiums), (f) underwriter service quality (claim processing time, communication), (g) recommendation for renewal, modification, or cancellation
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1414_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1414_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1414_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1414_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1414_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-287 (ensure controlled execution — AR &amp; Collections (PA-16.2).) | - operational: AR Supervisor review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: AR Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1414_Assoc17" sourceRef="W1414_Annotation16" targetRef="W1414_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
