    <bpmn:process id="W_W1420" name="W1420. Trade Account Monthly Statement Generation, Aging Analysis &amp; Field Collection Route Planning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly AR cycle (1st business day of the month); or weekly for high-risk accounts
Frequency: Monthly statement generation (all 5,200 trade accounts); weekly aging review (Watch and At-Risk accounts per W1200 segmentation); daily field collection visits for overdue accounts
Volume: ~5,200 trade accounts generating ~3,500 AR invoices/month; ~500–800 accounts in active collection at any time; ~30–50 field collection visits per week across all regions
Owner: AR Supervisor
Participants: AR Supervisor, Collection Officer, Trade Sales Manager, Regional Sales Coordinator, Controller
Source: workflow W1420 — Trade Account Monthly Statement Generation, Aging Analysis &amp; Field Collection Route Planning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1420_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1420_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1420_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1420_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1420_Lane2" name="AR Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1420_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1420_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1420_Lane3" name="Collection Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1420_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1420_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1420_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1420_Start5" name="Monthly AR cycle (1st business day of the month); or weekly for high-risk accounts">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1420_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1420_Task6" name="Monthly statement generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly statement generation (1st business day): System generates monthly statements for all 5,200 trade accounts: (a) opening balance, (b) invoices raised during month (with invoice number, date, amount, PO reference), (c) payments received during month, (d) closing balance, (e) payment due date per terms (Net 30 or Net 60), (f) statements emailed automatically to customer contact on file; hard copy mailed to customers without email (estimated ~10% of trade accounts)
Responsible (R): System / AR Clerk
Accountable (A): AR Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 hours (review + exception handling)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1420_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1420_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1420_Task7" name="Weekly aging analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Weekly aging analysis: AR Supervisor reviews weekly aging report: (a) current (0–30 days), (b) 31–60 days, (c) 61–90 days, (d) 90+ days, (e) identify accounts moving to next aging bucket — these are prioritized for collection, (f) compare to prior week: is overall AR health improving or deteriorating?
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1–2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1420_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1420_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1420_Task8" name="Collection prioritization and route planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Collection prioritization and route planning: Collection Officer plans weekly field collection route: (a) prioritize by: (i) accounts 90+ days overdue (highest priority), (ii) accounts moving from 60→90 days, (iii) accounts with broken payment promises, (iv) high-value accounts (&gt; PHP 500K overdue), (b) group visits by geographic area to minimize travel time (cluster customers by city/municipality), (c) schedule 6–8 visits per day per collection officer, (d) Trade Sales Manager provides customer relationship context (personal issues, project delays affecting payment)
Responsible (R): Collection Officer / Trade Sales Manager
Accountable (A): AR Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1420_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1420_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1420_Task9" name="Field collection execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Field collection execution: Collection Officer visits trade account customer: (a) present statement and discuss outstanding invoices, (b) obtain commitment: (i) specific payment date, (ii) partial payment collected on-site (cash or check), (iii) payment plan for large overdue amounts, (c) update collection notes in system: visit date, customer contact, commitment details, payment collected, (d) if customer refuses or is unreachable: escalate to W812 (field collection — formal demand)
Responsible (R): Collection Officer
Accountable (A): AR Supervisor
Duration: 6–8 visits/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1420_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1420_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1420_Task10" name="Collection performance tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Collection performance tracking: (a) AR Supervisor tracks weekly collection metrics: (i) total collections vs. target, (ii) DSO (days sales outstanding) trend, (iii) collection effectiveness index (CEI), (iv) field visit conversion rate (visits resulting in payment commitment), (b) Controller reviews monthly: are we on track to keep bad debt below 0.5% of trade revenue? (c) escalate to CFO if DSO exceeds 45 days for 2+ consecutive months
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1420_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1420_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
